## Dataset 1: Nigeria Administrative Boundaries

**Source:** DIVA GIS

**Source link:** [https://geodata.ucdavis.edu/diva/adm/NGA_adm.zip](https://geodata.ucdavis.edu/diva/adm/NGA_adm.zip)

**Number of features:** 37

**Geometry type:** Polygon

**Key columns:** `ID_0`, `ISO`, `NAME_0`, `ID_1`, `NAME_1`, `TYPE_1`, `ENGTYPE_1`

**Gaps or missing values:** `NL_NAME_1` and `VARNAME_1` contain missing (`NULL`) values.

**Purpose:** The dataset contains Nigeria's state-level administrative boundaries, representing the 36 states and the Federal Capital Territory. It is used to define the study area and support the spatial analysis of Ogun State.

## Dataset 2: Waterways

**Source:** OpenStreetMap (OSM), downloaded using the QuickOSM plugin in QGIS.

**Source link:** https://www.openstreetmap.org/

**Number of features:** 144

**Geometry type:** LineString

**Key columns:** `osm_id`, `osm_type`, `waterway`, `name_yo`, `width`, `seasonal`, `tidal`, `name`

**Gaps or missing values:** Some attribute fields contain missing values, particularly `name`, `width`, `seasonal`, and `tidal`, because not all mapped waterways have complete attribute information.

**Purpose:** The dataset contains mapped waterways across the study area and will be used to identify and represent water features that may support the classification and interpretation of land use and land cover in Ogun State.
